           question: "Why do cats purr?",
           answer:
             "Cats often purr when they feel relaxed, but they also use purring to self-soothe when stressed or recovering. <strong>Purring is not just a happiness signal</strong>; context like body posture and environment matters too.",
         },
         {
           question: "How much should I feed my cat each day?",
           answer:
             "The right amount depends on age, size, activity level, and whether the food is wet or dry. Use the food label as a starting point, then adjust with your veterinarian if your cat is gaining or losing weight too quickly.",
         },
         {
           question: "Why does my cat knead blankets or my lap?",
           answer:
             "Kneading is a kitten behavior linked to nursing, and many adult cats keep doing it because it feels comforting. It can also be a way to mark territory because scent glands in the paws leave behind a familiar smell.",
         },
         {
           question: "Do indoor cats still need enrichment?",
           answer:
             "Yes. Indoor cats benefit from climbing areas, scratching posts, puzzle feeders, window views, and short play sessions that mimic hunting. <strong>Enrichment helps reduce boredom-related behaviors</strong> like overgrooming or midnight zoomies.",
         },
         {
           question: "When should I worry about a hairball?",
           answer:
             "An occasional hairball can be normal, but repeated vomiting, constipation, loss of appetite, or frequent gagging deserves a veterinary check. Those signs can point to digestive issues instead of a simple grooming byproduct.",
         },
       ];

       const FAQItem = ({ question, answer, id }) => `
         <div class="example">
           <h3 class="question">
             <button
               type="button"
               class="trigger"
               aria-expanded="true"
               aria-controls="${id}"
             >
               <span class="trigger-text">${question}</span>
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h3>
           <div class="details" id="${id}">
             <p>${answer}</p>
           </div>
         </div>
       `;

       const FAQList = ({ items }) =>
         items
           .map((item, index) =>
             FAQItem({
               ...item,
               id: `answer-${index + 1}`,
             })
           )
           .join("");

       const App = () => `
         <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
           <div class="page-shell">
             <header class="hero">
               <p class="eyebrow">Cat care essentials</p>
               <h1>Frequently asked cat questions</h1>
               <p class="intro">
                 Quick answers for curious cat people, from everyday behavior to
                 healthy routines. Each question starts collapsed, so you can open
